{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DXJRg1xoqX52FBArMFrytE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — recursive_gen_depth_est\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n5\t- Backup: AAAI 2027 (abstract July 25, full paper August 1, 2026)\n6\t- EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" explicitly calls for work on data contamination, synthetic data feedback loops, and data governance — direct venue fit\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条 + Discussion implication)\n9\t\n10\t1. **Ordinal depth estimation is feasible, accurate, and robust across scales and generation modes**: Given text alone, recursive generation depth (d ∈ {0,1,2,...,K}) can be estimated with high accuracy using statistical features from reference-model perplexity distributions. On our 3-model × 3-strategy benchmark (1–1.5B), Random Forest classifiers on 19 statistical features achieve 70–85% four-class accuracy (chance=25%), with the best configuration (GPT-2 XL, temp τ=0.9) reaching 85.4%. Feature-based methods (RF, CORAL, DivEye) consistently outperform single-feature baselines across all settings. **Scale robustness**: Clean FP16 13B experiment (Qwen2.5-14B, no quantization) confirms depth signal persists at mainstream model scale, addressing the \"small model only\" concern from prior 7B QLoRA experiments. **Ecological validity**: Prompted generation experiment (topic-seeded text, not BOS-only unconditional) confirms depth signal is not an artifact of unnatural generation mode.\n11\t\n12\t2. **Depth Degradation Atlas — systematic characterization of recursive collapse** (PRIMARY): We provide the first systematic empirical characterization of how text statistical properties evolve across recursive generation depths, revealing (a) perplexity tail statistics (p90_ppl) and surprisal variance (var_surprisal) as the dominant depth signal family — consistently occupying the top-4 features across all models and strategies, though their relative ranking is model-dependent, (b) non-uniform inter-depth distances (depth 0→1 gap >> depth 2→3 gap), (c) an Effective Discriminable Depth (EDD) boundary beyond which adjacent depths become indistinguishable, and (d) **strategy-dependent feature trajectory reversal** — temperature sampling causes the depth-1→depth-2 feature boundary to invert relative to nucleus/top-k (cross-strategy LOO d1v2 AUC as low as 0.13), demonstrating that decoding strategy fundamentally shapes the degradation trajectory rather than merely attenuating it, and (e) **accelerated convergence mechanism** — root cause analysis confirms a genuine structural distributional shift: temperature's uniform logit scaling (vs nucleus/top-k truncation) accelerates convergence to the attractor distribution, so temp09 depth N features ≈ nucleus/topk50 depth N+1 (GPT-2 XL temp09 d1 p90_ppl median=92.2, falls into nucleus/topk50 d2 range 65–92). This is not a simple scale artifact fixable by normalization — z-score normalization improves overall LR cross-strategy accuracy (25%→61%) but does **not** recover pairwise d1v2 AUC (GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19), and does **not** improve tree-based classifiers (RF Δ<0.02pp) — confirming a distributional shift that simple feature normalization cannot resolve; whether more sophisticated domain adaptation methods could recover the d1/d2 boundary remains open. This atlas spans 3 model families × 3 decoding strategies, with scale consistency confirmed at 14B.\n13\t\n14\t3. **Cross-strategy depth estimation via two-stage pipeline**: Naive cross-strategy transfer degrades to 59.1% with d1v2 boundary inversion. We identify the root cause (temperature's accelerated convergence) and propose a practical two-stage solution: (a) strategy identification classifier using the same 19 features achieves [TBD]% accuracy, then (b) strategy-conditioned depth classifiers restore near within-strategy accuracy. This transforms the cross-strategy limitation from an open problem into a solved deployment challenge.\n15\t\n16\t4. **[Discussion — Practical Implication]** Depth-graduated curation as alternative to binary filtering: predicted depth provides a finer-grained quality proxy than binary real/synthetic labels, enabling graduated weighting strategies. Conceptual argument supported by depth-accuracy correlation in 3×3 matrix data; full experimental validation deferred to future work (D012).\n17\t\n18\t## Story Spine\n19\t\n20\t- **Problem**: Web-scraped training corpora increasingly contain multi-generational synthetic content from uncontrolled model→data→model feedback loops. Existing detectors answer \"is this synthetic?\" but not \"how many recursive cycles has this undergone?\" — a critical distinction since 1st-gen synthetic data can improve training while deeply recursive text drives distribution collapse.\n21\t\n22\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Binary detectors (LOKI, DivEye, Binoculars) classify real vs. synthetic but discard ordinal depth information. EditLens estimates single-pass AI editing extent but not recursive depth. Model collapse studies (Drayson et al. EMNLP 2025; Shumailov et al. Nature 2024) characterize degradation patterns but assume depth is known a priori — no method estimates depth from text alone.\n23\t\n24\t- **Our framing**: We formalize ordinal generation depth estimation as a new task, construct a multi-generational benchmark spanning 1B–14B models across 3 decoding strategies and 4 depths, and provide the first **Depth Degradation Atlas** — a systematic empirical map of how text statistical properties evolve across recursive depths, models, and strategies. The Atlas reveals (a) perplexity tail statistics as universal depth markers across all settings, (b) model-dependent strategy interaction effects with an identified root cause, and (c) the Effective Discriminable Depth (EDD) boundary beyond which adjacent depths become indistinguishable. We show that feature-based classifiers achieve 70–85% four-class accuracy, and propose a two-stage strategy-aware pipeline that solves the cross-strategy deployment challenge. The depth signal persists under prompted generation (not just BOS-seeded), confirming ecological relevance.\n25\t\n26\t- **Headline result template**: \"On our multi-generational benchmark spanning model scales from 1B to 14B and 3 decoding strategies, feature-based ordinal depth estimation achieves 70–85% accuracy (chance=25%), with perplexity tail statistics (p90_ppl, var_surprisal) consistently among the top-4 features across all settings. The depth signal persists under prompted (topic-seeded) generation and at 14B scale without quantization. The Depth Degradation Atlas reveals that effective discriminable depth extends to depth 3 in 7/9 settings (T=0.75). We identify strategy-dependent feature trajectory reversal and propose a two-stage pipeline that restores near within-strategy accuracy for cross-strategy deployment.\"\n27\t- **Note**: 4-class (depth 0-3) is the confirmed setting. 6-class (depth 0-5) completed via plan_011.\n28\t\n29\t## DCOL Status — Contingency Activated (D010/D011, 2026-05-15)\n30\t\n31\tDCOL v1–v5 全部失败（embedding collapse / OOM / catastrophic forgetting / 超参违规 / NaN 梯度爆炸）。\n32\t\n33\t- **Claim 2 (Atlas/EDD) 升为 PRIMARY contribution**\n34\t- **Claim 1**: Feature-based methods (RF/CORAL/DivEye) 作为 depth estimation 方法，不依赖 DCOL\n35\t- **DCOL v6 (RoBERTa-large)**: 非阻塞尝试。成功 → Section 5 bonus；失败 → negative analysis section（\"contrastive ordinal learning 在文本深度估计的固有局限\"）\n36\t- **Paper type**: Task formalization + systematic empirical study + practical framework（非 method paper）\n37\t- Atlas + EDD + feature universality + model-strategy interaction = 充分支撑 EMNLP \"New Missions\" track\n38\t\n39\t## Venue Fit Risks\n40\t\n41\t- **\"Just an empirical study\" risk**: Primary risk now that DCOL is demoted. Mitigation: (a) task formalization is a genuine contribution — no prior work estimates ordinal depth from text alone; (b) Atlas + EDD are novel analytical tools, not just tables; (c) feature universality finding (p90_ppl/var_surprisal top-4 across 9 settings) is a scientific claim with practical implications; (d) model-strategy interaction effects are a new finding; (e) **cross-strategy two-stage pipeline (Claim 3)** is a concrete practical contribution, not just analysis. EMNLP \"New Missions\" track explicitly values problem formalization.\n42\t- **Controlled vs wild gap**: Mitigation: prompted generation experiment validates signal under realistic generation conditions (topic-seeded, not BOS-only). Honest scoping — controlled setting is primary, prompted generation bridges toward ecological validity.\n43\t- **\"No novel method\" concern**: Mitigation: (a) RF/CORAL are tools, not the contribution; (b) the two-stage cross-strategy pipeline IS a novel practical method for strategy-aware depth estimation; (c) 13B clean experiment shows method scales without modification. Analogous to benchmark/analysis papers at top venues (e.g., HELM, MMLU).\n44\t- **\"Small model only\" concern**: Eliminated by clean 13B FP16 experiment. Prior 7B QLoRA results were contradictory due to quantization artifacts; 13B clean run provides definitive scale evidence.\n45\t\n46\t## Dream-Derived Requirements (D002, 2026-05-14)\n47\t\n48\t三档(best 3.0 / median 3.0 / worst 2.5)一致指出的结构性必修项：\n49\t\n50\t### 论文写作硬约束\n51\t1. **DCOL loss 描述** — 若 v6 成功：Eq.1 必须包含 attractive + repulsive 双项（N-pair formulation）。若 v6 失败：negative analysis section 描述失败模式和根因分析，无需完整 loss 公式\n52\t2. **至少4张图** — (a) AUC decay curve across depth pairs w/ EDD threshold line (b) feature trajectory panel (top-5 features × depth, stratified by model) (c) confusion matrix heatmap (d) Atlas feature×depth heatmap grid。\"Atlas without maps is a contradiction\"\n53\t3. **Bibliography 25+ references** — 必须覆盖: watermarking (Kirchenbauer ICML 2023), model collapse theory (Alemohammad ICLR 2024, Dohmatob 2024, Gerstgrasser 2024), data curation (DSIR, QuRating), multi-source attribution (Uchendu 2020), binary detectors (Binoculars Hans ICML 2024, Fast-DetectGPT Bao 2024), decoding strategy effects (Garces Arias COLING 2025, Holtzman ICLR 2020)\n54\t4. **Surprisal reference model** — 必须明确指定 reference model、说明 cross-model LOO 时如何处理、讨论 circularity\n55\t\n56\t### 指标报告硬约束\n57\t5. **d1-d5 only accuracy** — 作为 companion metric 报告，隔离 ordinal depth estimation 与 binary human-vs-machine detection\n58\t6. **EDD threshold sensitivity** — 报告 AUC threshold 在 0.65/0.70/0.75/0.80 四档下的 EDD 值\n59\t7. **k-NN inference 完整规格** — k 值、distance metric、sensitivity analysis\n60\t\n61\t### Framing 方向\n62\t8. **Atlas/EDD 为 primary contribution** — DCOL 定位为 \"one strong method within the framework\"，不作为 co-primary。三档审稿均认为 DCOL 是 incremental adaptation of CLOC。与 DCOL Contingency 一致。\n63\t9. **\"First systematic empirical map\" 需限定** — Shumailov/Drayson 已有 characterization, 我们的新颖性在 ordinal estimation lens + EDD formalization + multi-model multi-strategy coverage\n64\t\n65\t### Cross-Strategy 反转硬约束 (D015, Reviewer 降级条件)\n66\t10. **三档策略分类** — 论文不得将 nucleus 和 temperature 归为同一类 \"soft sampling\"。必须采用三档：nucleus（baseline 稳定）、temperature（信号增强但存在 d1v2 方向反转风险）、topk（信号衰减但方向一致）。D004 的 \"soft sampling\" 分组已被反转数据推翻。\n67\t11. **Discussion 必须含 per-strategy d1v2 AUC 表** — 包含 0.13/0.25 反转值 + **已确认的机制**：temperature 均匀缩放 logit（非截断）加速模型收敛到 attractor 分布（genuine structural distributional shift），temp09 depth N ≈ nucleus/topk50 depth N+1。z-score 标准化提升整体 LR 跨策略 acc（25%→61%）但**不恢复** pairwise d1v2 AUC（GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19），证实这是结构性几何偏移而非可校正的尺度差异。\n68\t12. **Limitations 必须写明跨策略部署约束** — \"跨策略部署时需先验知道目标策略类型，否则 d1/d2 预测可能反转。\"不可仅将反转作为正面发现消化。\n69\t\n70\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n71\t\n72\t1. \"EDD might be very low (depth 2-3), making the task trivial beyond shallow depths\" → Report EDD transparently; argue even low EDD is scientifically valuable (determines the boundary) and practically sufficient (shallow vs deep is the actionable distinction for curation). Data: 7/9 settings EDD≥3 at T=0.75. **Depth extension bootstrap (D027)**: 三模型 d3v4 AUC 聚集在 0.75 附近 (Pythia 0.784 p=0.001 ✅, OLMo 0.765 p=0.091 ⚠️, GPT-2 XL 0.750 p=0.505 ❌)，仅 Pythia 统计显著。**禁止**写 \"three models all achieve statistically significant EDD=4\"。正确措辞：\"d3v4 AUC consistently clusters near the 0.75 threshold (0.750–0.784) across all three models, while d4v5 AUC uniformly falls below 0.70 (0.681–0.694)\"——强调方向一致性 + 完整报告 CI 和 p-values。D024 连续衰减曲线叙事被 bootstrap 数据强力支持。\n73\t2. \"Why ordinal and not just binary?\" → d0v1 AUC=0.998 vs d1v2=0.861 vs d2v3=0.801 — ordinal structure captures monotonically decreasing but still significant discrimination at all adjacent pairs\n74\t3. \"Generalization to unseen models/strategies?\" → Cross-model LOO: mean 66.4% (holdout Pythia 62.4%, OLMo 69.2%, GPT-2 XL 67.6%) — all >chance but depth_0 recall >98% inflates headline. **Must report per-class recall** (depth_2 recall as low as 26.8%). Cross-strategy LOO: mean 59.1% (51.5–69.4%), topk50 holdout consistently worst. **temp09 holdout shows d1v2 AUC reversal** (GPT-2 XL 0.13, OLMo 0.25) — root cause confirmed as genuine structural distributional shift (temperature accelerates convergence to attractor distribution). Z-score normalization improves overall LR acc (25%→61%) but does **not** recover pairwise d1v2 AUC (GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19), confirming a distributional shift that simple feature normalization cannot resolve; whether more sophisticated domain adaptation could recover d1v2 AUC remains open. Discuss as \"strategy shapes degradation trajectory\" finding — temp09 cross-strategy d1v2 generalization remains an open problem (D013/D015/D021).\n75\t4. \"No novel method — just RF on features\" → (a) Contribution is task formalization + Atlas + EDD + systematic findings, not just method; (b) the two-stage cross-strategy pipeline (Claim 3) IS a novel practical method that solves the deployment challenge; (c) 13B clean experiment confirms the approach scales without modification. Analogous to benchmark papers (HELM, MMLU). Feature universality across 9+ settings is itself a finding.\n76\t5. \"d0 confound inflates headline metrics\" → Report d1-only accuracy alongside full accuracy; 3-class (d1/d2/d3) results already show 59–82% accuracy\n77\t6. \"EDD threshold is arbitrary\" → Sensitivity analysis at 0.65/0.70/0.75/0.80 completed (Dream D002)\n78\t7. \"No figures for Atlas\" → Minimum 4 figures (Dream D002)\n79\t8. \"Bibliography too thin\" → 25+ refs covering all relevant subfields (Dream D002)\n80\t9. \"Model-strategy interaction is just noise\" → Three-tier pattern confirmed: nucleus=stable baseline, temperature=enhances signal but reverses d1v2 feature boundary in cross-strategy transfer, topk=attenuates signal but preserves direction (D015). Garces Arias (COLING 2025) independently confirms model-dependent strategy effects.\n81\t10. \"Cross-strategy deployment is unreliable\" → **Now addressed by Claim 3**: Two-stage pipeline (strategy identification → strategy-conditioned depth classification) provides a practical solution. Strategy classifier expected >90% accuracy on 19 features (strategy distributions are highly separable). After strategy identification, depth classification uses strategy-matched RF, restoring near within-strategy accuracy. The root cause (temperature's accelerated convergence) is identified and the mechanism explained — this is no longer an open problem but a solved deployment challenge.\n82\t11. \"Signal is an artifact of unconditional BOS-seeded generation\" → Prompted generation experiment (plan_016) tests depth signal under topic-seeded generation. If signal persists → validates ecological relevance; if not → important finding about generation mode dependence (written as limitation).\n83\t12. \"Only tested on small models (1–1.5B)\" → Clean 13B FP16 experiment (Qwen2.5-14B, plan_017) confirms scale robustness without quantization confounds. Prior 7B QLoRA results were contradictory — now superseded by clean experiment.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e0d3815-f5c2-419a-a028-0e345e283d74","uuid":"3b9ce755-707c-48a5-994a-2950afd99e0b","timestamp":"2026-05-17T08:37:15.888Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_2/projects/recursive_gen_depth_est/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T075852/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — recursive_gen_depth_est\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (ARR May 25, 2026)\n- Backup: AAAI 2027 (abstract July 25, full paper August 1, 2026)\n- EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" explicitly calls for work on data contamination, synthetic data feedback loops, and data governance — direct venue fit\n\n## Core Claims (3 条 + Discussion implication)\n\n1. **Ordinal depth estimation is feasible, accurate, and robust across scales and generation modes**: Given text alone, recursive generation depth (d ∈ {0,1,2,...,K}) can be estimated with high accuracy using statistical features from reference-model perplexity distributions. On our 3-model × 3-strategy benchmark (1–1.5B), Random Forest classifiers on 19 statistical features achieve 70–85% four-class accuracy (chance=25%), with the best configuration (GPT-2 XL, temp τ=0.9) reaching 85.4%. Feature-based methods (RF, CORAL, DivEye) consistently outperform single-feature baselines across all settings. **Scale robustness**: Clean FP16 13B experiment (Qwen2.5-14B, no quantization) confirms depth signal persists at mainstream model scale, addressing the \"small model only\" concern from prior 7B QLoRA experiments. **Ecological validity**: Prompted generation experiment (topic-seeded text, not BOS-only unconditional) confirms depth signal is not an artifact of unnatural generation mode.\n\n2. **Depth Degradation Atlas — systematic characterization of recursive collapse** (PRIMARY): We provide the first systematic empirical characterization of how text statistical properties evolve across recursive generation depths, revealing (a) perplexity tail statistics (p90_ppl) and surprisal variance (var_surprisal) as the dominant depth signal family — consistently occupying the top-4 features across all models and strategies, though their relative ranking is model-dependent, (b) non-uniform inter-depth distances (depth 0→1 gap >> depth 2→3 gap), (c) an Effective Discriminable Depth (EDD) boundary beyond which adjacent depths become indistinguishable, and (d) **strategy-dependent feature trajectory reversal** — temperature sampling causes the depth-1→depth-2 feature boundary to invert relative to nucleus/top-k (cross-strategy LOO d1v2 AUC as low as 0.13), demonstrating that decoding strategy fundamentally shapes the degradation trajectory rather than merely attenuating it, and (e) **accelerated convergence mechanism** — root cause analysis confirms a genuine structural distributional shift: temperature's uniform logit scaling (vs nucleus/top-k truncation) accelerates convergence to the attractor distribution, so temp09 depth N features ≈ nucleus/topk50 depth N+1 (GPT-2 XL temp09 d1 p90_ppl median=92.2, falls into nucleus/topk50 d2 range 65–92). This is not a simple scale artifact fixable by normalization — z-score normalization improves overall LR cross-strategy accuracy (25%→61%) but does **not** recover pairwise d1v2 AUC (GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19), and does **not** improve tree-based classifiers (RF Δ<0.02pp) — confirming a distributional shift that simple feature normalization cannot resolve; whether more sophisticated domain adaptation methods could recover the d1/d2 boundary remains open. This atlas spans 3 model families × 3 decoding strategies, with scale consistency confirmed at 14B.\n\n3. **Cross-strategy depth estimation via two-stage pipeline**: Naive cross-strategy transfer degrades to 59.1% with d1v2 boundary inversion. We identify the root cause (temperature's accelerated convergence) and propose a practical two-stage solution: (a) strategy identification classifier using the same 19 features achieves [TBD]% accuracy, then (b) strategy-conditioned depth classifiers restore near within-strategy accuracy. This transforms the cross-strategy limitation from an open problem into a solved deployment challenge.\n\n4. **[Discussion — Practical Implication]** Depth-graduated curation as alternative to binary filtering: predicted depth provides a finer-grained quality proxy than binary real/synthetic labels, enabling graduated weighting strategies. Conceptual argument supported by depth-accuracy correlation in 3×3 matrix data; full experimental validation deferred to future work (D012).\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: Web-scraped training corpora increasingly contain multi-generational synthetic content from uncontrolled model→data→model feedback loops. Existing detectors answer \"is this synthetic?\" but not \"how many recursive cycles has this undergone?\" — a critical distinction since 1st-gen synthetic data can improve training while deeply recursive text drives distribution collapse.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Binary detectors (LOKI, DivEye, Binoculars) classify real vs. synthetic but discard ordinal depth information. EditLens estimates single-pass AI editing extent but not recursive depth. Model collapse studies (Drayson et al. EMNLP 2025; Shumailov et al. Nature 2024) characterize degradation patterns but assume depth is known a priori — no method estimates depth from text alone.\n\n- **Our framing**: We formalize ordinal generation depth estimation as a new task, construct a multi-generational benchmark spanning 1B–14B models across 3 decoding strategies and 4 depths, and provide the first **Depth Degradation Atlas** — a systematic empirical map of how text statistical properties evolve across recursive depths, models, and strategies. The Atlas reveals (a) perplexity tail statistics as universal depth markers across all settings, (b) model-dependent strategy interaction effects with an identified root cause, and (c) the Effective Discriminable Depth (EDD) boundary beyond which adjacent depths become indistinguishable. We show that feature-based classifiers achieve 70–85% four-class accuracy, and propose a two-stage strategy-aware pipeline that solves the cross-strategy deployment challenge. The depth signal persists under prompted generation (not just BOS-seeded), confirming ecological relevance.\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"On our multi-generational benchmark spanning model scales from 1B to 14B and 3 decoding strategies, feature-based ordinal depth estimation achieves 70–85% accuracy (chance=25%), with perplexity tail statistics (p90_ppl, var_surprisal) consistently among the top-4 features across all settings. The depth signal persists under prompted (topic-seeded) generation and at 14B scale without quantization. The Depth Degradation Atlas reveals that effective discriminable depth extends to depth 3 in 7/9 settings (T=0.75). We identify strategy-dependent feature trajectory reversal and propose a two-stage pipeline that restores near within-strategy accuracy for cross-strategy deployment.\"\n- **Note**: 4-class (depth 0-3) is the confirmed setting. 6-class (depth 0-5) completed via plan_011.\n\n## DCOL Status — Contingency Activated (D010/D011, 2026-05-15)\n\nDCOL v1–v5 全部失败（embedding collapse / OOM / catastrophic forgetting / 超参违规 / NaN 梯度爆炸）。\n\n- **Claim 2 (Atlas/EDD) 升为 PRIMARY contribution**\n- **Claim 1**: Feature-based methods (RF/CORAL/DivEye) 作为 depth estimation 方法，不依赖 DCOL\n- **DCOL v6 (RoBERTa-large)**: 非阻塞尝试。成功 → Section 5 bonus；失败 → negative analysis section（\"contrastive ordinal learning 在文本深度估计的固有局限\"）\n- **Paper type**: Task formalization + systematic empirical study + practical framework（非 method paper）\n- Atlas + EDD + feature universality + model-strategy interaction = 充分支撑 EMNLP \"New Missions\" track\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n\n- **\"Just an empirical study\" risk**: Primary risk now that DCOL is demoted. Mitigation: (a) task formalization is a genuine contribution — no prior work estimates ordinal depth from text alone; (b) Atlas + EDD are novel analytical tools, not just tables; (c) feature universality finding (p90_ppl/var_surprisal top-4 across 9 settings) is a scientific claim with practical implications; (d) model-strategy interaction effects are a new finding; (e) **cross-strategy two-stage pipeline (Claim 3)** is a concrete practical contribution, not just analysis. EMNLP \"New Missions\" track explicitly values problem formalization.\n- **Controlled vs wild gap**: Mitigation: prompted generation experiment validates signal under realistic generation conditions (topic-seeded, not BOS-only). Honest scoping — controlled setting is primary, prompted generation bridges toward ecological validity.\n- **\"No novel method\" concern**: Mitigation: (a) RF/CORAL are tools, not the contribution; (b) the two-stage cross-strategy pipeline IS a novel practical method for strategy-aware depth estimation; (c) 13B clean experiment shows method scales without modification. Analogous to benchmark/analysis papers at top venues (e.g., HELM, MMLU).\n- **\"Small model only\" concern**: Eliminated by clean 13B FP16 experiment. Prior 7B QLoRA results were contradictory due to quantization artifacts; 13B clean run provides definitive scale evidence.\n\n## Dream-Derived Requirements (D002, 2026-05-14)\n\n三档(best 3.0 / median 3.0 / worst 2.5)一致指出的结构性必修项：\n\n### 论文写作硬约束\n1. **DCOL loss 描述** — 若 v6 成功：Eq.1 必须包含 attractive + repulsive 双项（N-pair formulation）。若 v6 失败：negative analysis section 描述失败模式和根因分析，无需完整 loss 公式\n2. **至少4张图** — (a) AUC decay curve across depth pairs w/ EDD threshold line (b) feature trajectory panel (top-5 features × depth, stratified by model) (c) confusion matrix heatmap (d) Atlas feature×depth heatmap grid。\"Atlas without maps is a contradiction\"\n3. **Bibliography 25+ references** — 必须覆盖: watermarking (Kirchenbauer ICML 2023), model collapse theory (Alemohammad ICLR 2024, Dohmatob 2024, Gerstgrasser 2024), data curation (DSIR, QuRating), multi-source attribution (Uchendu 2020), binary detectors (Binoculars Hans ICML 2024, Fast-DetectGPT Bao 2024), decoding strategy effects (Garces Arias COLING 2025, Holtzman ICLR 2020)\n4. **Surprisal reference model** — 必须明确指定 reference model、说明 cross-model LOO 时如何处理、讨论 circularity\n\n### 指标报告硬约束\n5. **d1-d5 only accuracy** — 作为 companion metric 报告，隔离 ordinal depth estimation 与 binary human-vs-machine detection\n6. **EDD threshold sensitivity** — 报告 AUC threshold 在 0.65/0.70/0.75/0.80 四档下的 EDD 值\n7. **k-NN inference 完整规格** — k 值、distance metric、sensitivity analysis\n\n### Framing 方向\n8. **Atlas/EDD 为 primary contribution** — DCOL 定位为 \"one strong method within the framework\"，不作为 co-primary。三档审稿均认为 DCOL 是 incremental adaptation of CLOC。与 DCOL Contingency 一致。\n9. **\"First systematic empirical map\" 需限定** — Shumailov/Drayson 已有 characterization, 我们的新颖性在 ordinal estimation lens + EDD formalization + multi-model multi-strategy coverage\n\n### Cross-Strategy 反转硬约束 (D015, Reviewer 降级条件)\n10. **三档策略分类** — 论文不得将 nucleus 和 temperature 归为同一类 \"soft sampling\"。必须采用三档：nucleus（baseline 稳定）、temperature（信号增强但存在 d1v2 方向反转风险）、topk（信号衰减但方向一致）。D004 的 \"soft sampling\" 分组已被反转数据推翻。\n11. **Discussion 必须含 per-strategy d1v2 AUC 表** — 包含 0.13/0.25 反转值 + **已确认的机制**：temperature 均匀缩放 logit（非截断）加速模型收敛到 attractor 分布（genuine structural distributional shift），temp09 depth N ≈ nucleus/topk50 depth N+1。z-score 标准化提升整体 LR 跨策略 acc（25%→61%）但**不恢复** pairwise d1v2 AUC（GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19），证实这是结构性几何偏移而非可校正的尺度差异。\n12. **Limitations 必须写明跨策略部署约束** — \"跨策略部署时需先验知道目标策略类型，否则 d1/d2 预测可能反转。\"不可仅将反转作为正面发现消化。\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. \"EDD might be very low (depth 2-3), making the task trivial beyond shallow depths\" → Report EDD transparently; argue even low EDD is scientifically valuable (determines the boundary) and practically sufficient (shallow vs deep is the actionable distinction for curation). Data: 7/9 settings EDD≥3 at T=0.75. **Depth extension bootstrap (D027)**: 三模型 d3v4 AUC 聚集在 0.75 附近 (Pythia 0.784 p=0.001 ✅, OLMo 0.765 p=0.091 ⚠️, GPT-2 XL 0.750 p=0.505 ❌)，仅 Pythia 统计显著。**禁止**写 \"three models all achieve statistically significant EDD=4\"。正确措辞：\"d3v4 AUC consistently clusters near the 0.75 threshold (0.750–0.784) across all three models, while d4v5 AUC uniformly falls below 0.70 (0.681–0.694)\"——强调方向一致性 + 完整报告 CI 和 p-values。D024 连续衰减曲线叙事被 bootstrap 数据强力支持。\n2. \"Why ordinal and not just binary?\" → d0v1 AUC=0.998 vs d1v2=0.861 vs d2v3=0.801 — ordinal structure captures monotonically decreasing but still significant discrimination at all adjacent pairs\n3. \"Generalization to unseen models/strategies?\" → Cross-model LOO: mean 66.4% (holdout Pythia 62.4%, OLMo 69.2%, GPT-2 XL 67.6%) — all >chance but depth_0 recall >98% inflates headline. **Must report per-class recall** (depth_2 recall as low as 26.8%). Cross-strategy LOO: mean 59.1% (51.5–69.4%), topk50 holdout consistently worst. **temp09 holdout shows d1v2 AUC reversal** (GPT-2 XL 0.13, OLMo 0.25) — root cause confirmed as genuine structural distributional shift (temperature accelerates convergence to attractor distribution). Z-score normalization improves overall LR acc (25%→61%) but does **not** recover pairwise d1v2 AUC (GPT-2 XL 0.50→0.24, OLMo 0.50→0.19), confirming a distributional shift that simple feature normalization cannot resolve; whether more sophisticated domain adaptation could recover d1v2 AUC remains open. Discuss as \"strategy shapes degradation trajectory\" finding — temp09 cross-strategy d1v2 generalization remains an open problem (D013/D015/D021).\n4. \"No novel method — just RF on features\" → (a) Contribution is task formalization + Atlas + EDD + systematic findings, not just method; (b) the two-stage cross-strategy pipeline (Claim 3) IS a novel practical method that solves the deployment challenge; (c) 13B clean experiment confirms the approach scales without modification. Analogous to benchmark papers (HELM, MMLU). Feature universality across 9+ settings is itself a finding.\n5. \"d0 confound inflates headline metrics\" → Report d1-only accuracy alongside full accuracy; 3-class (d1/d2/d3) results already show 59–82% accuracy\n6. \"EDD threshold is arbitrary\" → Sensitivity analysis at 0.65/0.70/0.75/0.80 completed (Dream D002)\n7. \"No figures for Atlas\" → Minimum 4 figures (Dream D002)\n8. \"Bibliography too thin\" → 25+ refs covering all relevant subfields (Dream D002)\n9. \"Model-strategy interaction is just noise\" → Three-tier pattern confirmed: nucleus=stable baseline, temperature=enhances signal but reverses d1v2 feature boundary in cross-strategy transfer, topk=attenuates signal but preserves direction (D015). Garces Arias (COLING 2025) independently confirms model-dependent strategy effects.\n10. \"Cross-strategy deployment is unreliable\" → **Now addressed by Claim 3**: Two-stage pipeline (strategy identification → strategy-conditioned depth classification) provides a practical solution. Strategy classifier expected >90% accuracy on 19 features (strategy distributions are highly separable). After strategy identification, depth classification uses strategy-matched RF, restoring near within-strategy accuracy. The root cause (temperature's accelerated convergence) is identified and the mechanism explained — this is no longer an open problem but a solved deployment challenge.\n11. \"Signal is an artifact of unconditional BOS-seeded generation\" → Prompted generation experiment (plan_016) tests depth signal under topic-seeded generation. If signal persists → validates ecological relevance; if not → important finding about generation mode dependence (written as limitation).\n12. \"Only tested on small models (1–1.5B)\" → Clean 13B FP16 experiment (Qwen2.5-14B, plan_017) confirms scale robustness without quantization confounds. Prior 7B QLoRA results were contradictory — now superseded by clean experiment.\n","numLines":84,"startLine":1,"totalLines":84}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BgSfht953MKFVSsd11brRr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"DCOL component ablation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"DCOL v6 (RoBERTa-large) 失败后前置条件 plan_004 未满足，此实验已取消。\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"status\": \"cancelled\",\n7\t      \"reason\": \"DCOL v6 conclusion=negative (test_acc=64.5% vs RF baseline 78.2%, -13.7pp)，无可消融的成功模型\"\n8\t    },\n9\t    \"tables\": [],\n10\t    \"figures\": [],\n11\t    \"analysis\": \"plan_010 取消对论文无影响。DCOL 失败本身写入 negative analysis section（约 0.5 页）， 论述\\\"为何 contrastive ordinal learning 在此 task 上比 feature engineering 差\\\"。 这反而强化 Atlas（Claim 2）的 primary 定位——统计特征方法的优越性不是因为缺乏更好方法， 而是因为任务特性（稀疏信号、微弱梯度）使端到端学习困难。\\n\\n\\nDCOL v1-v6 全线失败，最好结果仅 64.5%（RoBERTa-large v6），远低于 RF baseline。 contrastive ordinal learning 在文本深度估计上存在固有困难：(1) 文本嵌入空间的深度梯度 远弱于 19 维统计特征空间中的梯度，(2) 端到端学习需要从原始文本中同时学习特征提取和序数 排列，数据量不足以支撑。消融无意义——没有成功的完整模型可以消融。\\n\"\n12\t  },\n13\t  {\n14\t    \"name\": \"13B clean FP16 scale validation (Qwen2.5-14B)\",\n15\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-14B FP16 + LoRA on 96GB RTX PRO 6000，nucleus p=0.95 decoding， d0-d3 递归链 + Pythia-160M reference model 19 特征提取 + RF/LR 分类。 验证 depth signal 在主流模型规模上是否持续。\\n\",\n16\t    \"results\": {\n17\t      \"four_class_acc_rf\": 0.55,\n18\t      \"four_class_acc_rf_ci\": [\n19\t        0.53,\n20\t        0.57\n21\t      ],\n22\t      \"four_class_acc_lr\": 0.51,\n23\t      \"d0v1_auc\": 0.96,\n24\t      \"d1v2_auc\": 0.62,\n25\t      \"d2v3_auc\": 0.56,\n26\t      \"d1v3_auc\": 0.81,\n27\t      \"three_class_acc\": 0.44,\n28\t      \"three_class_acc_ci\": [\n29\t        0.42,\n30\t        0.46\n31\t      ],\n32\t      \"edd_at_075\": 1,\n33\t      \"edd_at_070\": 2,\n34\t      \"feature_top2_in_top4\": false,\n35\t      \"top_features_predicted\": [\n36\t        \"mean_ppl\",\n37\t        \"p75_ppl\",\n38\t        \"type_token_ratio\",\n39\t        \"rep_3gram\",\n40\t        \"p90_ppl\"\n41\t      ],\n42\t      \"u_shape_artifact\": true,\n43\t      \"u_shape_pattern\": \"d1v2=0.62, d2v3=0.56 (trough), possible d2v3 < d3v4 recovery\",\n44\t      \"finetune_loss_d0\": 1.85,\n45\t      \"finetune_loss_d1\": 1.52,\n46\t      \"finetune_loss_d2\": 1.38,\n47\t      \"finetune_loss_d3\": 1.31,\n48\t      \"loss_convergence_gap_d1_d2\": 0.14,\n49\t      \"per_class_recall\": {\n50\t        \"d0\": 0.93,\n51\t        \"d1\": 0.48,\n52\t        \"d2\": 0.32,\n53\t        \"d3\": 0.47\n54\t      },\n55\t      \"acc_vs_best_1_5b_retention_pct\": 64.4\n56\t    },\n57\t    \"tables\": [\n58\t      {\n59\t        \"name\": \"Table S1: 13B vs 1-1.5B 4-class accuracy comparison\",\n60\t        \"columns\": [\n61\t          \"model\",\n62\t          \"scale\",\n63\t          \"4class_acc_rf\",\n64\t          \"d1v2_auc\",\n65\t          \"d2v3_auc\",\n66\t          \"edd_075\"\n67\t        ],\n68\t        \"rows\": [\n69\t          [\n70\t            \"Pythia-1.4B\",\n71\t            \"1.4B\",\n72\t            0.782,\n73\t            0.861,\n74\t            0.801,\n75\t            3\n76\t          ],\n77\t          [\n78\t            \"OLMo-1B\",\n79\t            \"1B\",\n80\t            0.788,\n81\t            0.867,\n82\t            0.812,\n83\t            3\n84\t          ],\n85\t          [\n86\t            \"GPT-2 XL\",\n87\t            \"1.5B\",\n88\t            0.833,\n89\t            0.913,\n90\t            0.883,\n91\t            3\n92\t          ],\n93\t          [\n94\t            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n95\t            \"14B\",\n96\t            0.55,\n97\t            0.62,\n98\t            0.56,\n99\t            1\n100\t          ],\n101\t          [\n102\t            \"Qwen-7B (QLoRA ref)\",\n103\t            \"7B\",\n104\t            0.601,\n105\t            0.729,\n106\t            0.709,\n107\t            \">5 (U-shape)\"\n108\t          ]\n109\t        ]\n110\t      },\n111\t      {\n112\t        \"name\": \"Table S2: 13B feature importance vs 1-1.5B consensus\",\n113\t        \"columns\": [\n114\t          \"rank\",\n115\t          \"1-1.5B consensus\",\n116\t          \"13B predicted\"\n117\t        ],\n118\t        \"rows\": [\n119\t          [\n120\t            1,\n121\t            \"p90_ppl / var_surprisal\",\n122\t            \"mean_ppl\"\n123\t          ],\n124\t          [\n125\t            2,\n126\t            \"var_surprisal / p90_ppl\",\n127\t            \"p75_ppl\"\n128\t          ],\n129\t          [\n130\t            3,\n131\t            \"mean_ppl / p75_ppl\",\n132\t            \"type_token_ratio\"\n133\t          ],\n134\t          [\n135\t            4,\n136\t            \"mean_surprisal\",\n137\t            \"rep_3gram\"\n138\t          ],\n139\t          [\n140\t            5,\n141\t            \"p75_ppl / mean_ppl\",\n142\t            \"p90_ppl\"\n143\t          ]\n144\t        ]\n145\t      }\n146\t    ],\n147\t    \"figures\": [],\n148\t    \"analysis\": \"13B 结果证实 worst tier 核心假设：Pythia reference model 对大规模模型输出的 perplexity 特征区分力本质受限。55% 4-class accuracy 虽然显著高于 chance（25%）， 但相比 1-1.5B 的 70-85% 有 >20pp 衰减。更关键的是 EDD=1，意味着 ordinal depth estimation 在 13B 条件下实质退化为 binary detection。\\n叙事处理：此结果不写入 Limitations，而是写入 Section 6 \\\"Boundary Conditions\\\" 的 Scale Dimension 子节。结论：\\\"feature-based depth estimation captures a real signal at 14B scale (55% vs 25% chance, p<0.001), but the signal is severely attenuated compared to 1-1.5B, with EDD collapsing from 3 to 1. The primary bottleneck is the cross-scale perplexity measurement gap: a 160M reference model's perplexity landscape compresses the depth gradient of 14B outputs.\\\"\\n这为 future work 指出明确方向：(1) scale-matched reference models（用 7B 作为 14B 的 reference），(2) reference-free features（但 reference_free_baseline_001 已证明 reference-free 在 1-1.5B 上就差 25pp），(3) 直接使用 14B 自身的 internal representations 而非外部 perplexity。\\n\\n\\nWorst tier 核心机制：Pythia-160M reference model 对 14B 输出的 perplexity 特征 区分力严重不足。14B 模型的词汇分布远比 1-1.5B 复杂——Pythia-160M 对所有 14B 输出 都给出极高 perplexity（因为 14B 的选词模式超出 160M 的建模能力），导致 p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 的深度梯度被压缩到一个高 perplexity plateau 上，信噪比骤降。\\n具体机制链：(1) Qwen2.5-14B 的 BPE 词表（151K tokens）与 Pythia 词表（50K tokens） 不匹配，Pythia 需要更多 subword tokens 来编码 14B 的输出，系统性地膨胀 perplexity baseline；(2) 14B 模型容量大，LoRA rank=16 的微调在每个深度迭代中只轻微扰动模型—— finetune loss 序列 1.85→1.52→1.38→1.31 的衰减斜率远小于 1-1.5B 的 2.2→1.4→1.0， 说明 14B 的 LoRA 适配器修改的分布偏移量远小于小模型；(3) 由于每步分布偏移小， Pythia 测量到的深度间特征差异在噪声水平附近——d1v2 AUC 仅 0.62，d2v3 仅 0.56。\\nU-shape artifact 的来源：与 Qwen 7B（cross_scale_qwen7b_001, U-shape confirmed） 同源。d2v3 出现 trough 是因为 depth-2 和 depth-3 的 LoRA 叠加效应使模型在某些 高频 token 上出现非单调的 logit 变化，Pythia 的 perplexity 在这些位置产生混淆信号。 Llama3 8B base 也出现了 U-shape（d2v3=0.68, d3v4=0.73 recovery），进一步支持 这是跨规模特征迁移的系统性问题而非 Qwen 特有。\\nFeature importance 结构破坏：p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 不再占据 top-2，因为在高 perplexity plateau 上，尾部统计量的信噪比下降最快。mean_ppl 和 p75_ppl 因为 信号更平滑反而排名上升，但整体区分力弱。\\nEDD=1（T=0.75）意味着只有 d0v1 可靠区分，即 13B 条件下 depth estimation 实质 退化为 binary real-vs-synthetic detection。\\n\"\n149\t  },\n150\t  {\n151\t    \"name\": \"Wild-data calibration on RedPajama/Dolma\",\n152\t    \"description\": \"在 RedPajama 和 Dolma 真实 web 数据上评估训练好的 depth classifiers 的 calibration 和 false positive rate。验证 controlled-setting 训练的分类器在 wild data 上的可靠性。\\n\",\n153\t    \"results\": {\n154\t      \"redpajama_n_passages\": 5000,\n155\t      \"redpajama_d0_pct\": 72.0,\n156\t      \"redpajama_fpr_pct\": 28.0,\n157\t      \"redpajama_d1_pct\": 18.5,\n158\t      \"redpajama_d2_pct\": 5.8,\n159\t      \"redpajama_d3_pct\": 3.7,\n160\t      \"dolma_n_passages\": 5000,\n161\t      \"dolma_d0_pct\": 76.5,\n162\t      \"dolma_fpr_pct\": 23.5,\n163\t      \"dolma_d1_pct\": 16.2,\n164\t      \"dolma_d2_pct\": 4.3,\n165\t      \"dolma_d3_pct\": 3.0,\n166\t      \"cross_model_fpr_range_pp\": 18,\n167\t      \"mean_p_d0_redpajama\": 0.68,\n168\t      \"mean_p_d0_dolma\": 0.72,\n169\t      \"pythia_fpr\": 28.0,\n170\t      \"gpt2xl_fpr\": 30.5,\n171\t      \"olmo_fpr\": 12.0,\n172\t      \"calibration_brier_score\": 0.28\n173\t    },\n174\t    \"tables\": [\n175\t      {\n176\t        \"name\": \"Table S3: Wild-data FPR across datasets and reference models\",\n177\t        \"columns\": [\n178\t          \"dataset\",\n179\t          \"pythia_fpr\",\n180\t          \"gpt2xl_fpr\",\n181\t          \"olmo_fpr\",\n182\t          \"mean_fpr\"\n183\t        ],\n184\t        \"rows\": [\n185\t          [\n186\t            \"WikiText-103\",\n187\t            0.0,\n188\t            1.4,\n189\t            1.5,\n190\t            1.0\n191\t          ],\n192\t          [\n193\t            \"OpenWebText\",\n194\t            0.9,\n195\t            1.4,\n196\t            2.8,\n197\t            1.7\n198\t          ],\n199\t          [\n200\t            \"C4\",\n201\t            20.2,\n202\t            22.4,\n203\t            4.7,\n204\t            15.8\n205\t          ],\n206\t          [\n207\t            \"FineWeb\",\n208\t            19.5,\n209\t            \"~20\",\n210\t            \"~5\",\n211\t            \"~15\"\n212\t          ],\n213\t          [\n214\t            \"RedPajama (predicted)\",\n215\t            28.0,\n216\t            30.5,\n217\t            12.0,\n218\t            23.5\n219\t          ],\n220\t          [\n221\t            \"Dolma (predicted)\",\n222\t            25.0,\n223\t            27.0,\n224\t            10.0,\n225\t            20.7\n226\t          ]\n227\t        ]\n228\t      }\n229\t    ],\n230\t    \"figures\": [],\n231\t    \"analysis\": \"Wild-data 结果在 worst tier 下强化 \\\"boundary conditions\\\" 叙事的第四维度： domain shift。Controlled-setting 分类器在 editorial-quality 数据上表现优异 （WikiText FPR<2%），但在 web-crawl 数据上 FPR 高达 23-30%，且 reference model 依赖性强。\\n这不会进入论文主体（plan_015 延后到 AAAI），但如果包含，应写入 Section 6 \\\"Boundary Conditions\\\" 的 Domain Dimension：depth signal 的第四个衰减边界。 与 scale（>1.5B attenuation）、generation mode（prompted attenuation）、 depth（EDD=4）并列。\\n对 EMNLP 投稿的影响：不纳入此实验是正确决策。Wild-data calibration 的复杂度 足以支撑一篇独立 follow-up 论文，强行塞入当前论文会分散 Atlas 核心贡献的注意力。\\n\\n\\nWorst tier 预期 FPR 在 23-30% 范围，与已有 wild data 结果一致但偏高端。\\n机制分析：(1) RedPajama 包含大量 CommonCrawl 数据，其中 template content、 SEO 文本、自动生成的产品描述占比显著。这些文本的统计特征（高 rep_3gram/rep_4gram、 低 type_token_ratio、异常 p90_ppl）与递归生成文本在特征空间中重叠，导致误分类。 已有证据：C4 FPR=20.2%（Pythia）、FineWeb FPR=19.5%，但 RedPajama 的 CommonCrawl 质量过滤比 C4 更宽松，预期 FPR 更高。\\n(2) Dolma 由 AI2 策划，含 CommonCrawl + Wikipedia + Books + GitHub + arXiv 等 多域混合。Wikipedia/Books 子集 FPR 极低（参考 WikiText 0% FPR），但 CommonCrawl 子集拉高整体 FPR。混合后预期 FPR ~23.5%。\\n(3) Cross-model FPR 一致性差（range=18pp）是因为不同 reference model 的 perplexity landscape 对 web 噪声的敏感度不同——OLMo 在 Dolma 上训练（域匹配），FPR 较低（参考 olmo_calibration_001 C4 FPR=4.7%），而 Pythia/GPT-2 XL 域失配导致 FPR 飙升。\\n(4) Calibration 差（Brier score 0.28）说明分类器的置信度在 wild data 上不可靠， 限制了任何基于预测概率的 graduated curation 方案。\\n这些结果证实：controlled-setting 训练的分类器在 wild data 部署面临严重的 domain shift 问题，FPR 的高方差（12-30% 取决于 reference model）使得实际部署需要 domain-specific calibration，大幅限制了 Claim 1 的 practical applicability。\\n\"\n232\t  },\n233\t  {\n234\t    \"name\": \"Prompted generation ecological validity (GPT-2 XL, topic-seeded)\",\n235\t    \"description\": \"GPT-2 XL nucleus p=0.95，用 topic prompt 前缀（\\\"The following article discusses...\\\"等） 生成 d0，LoRA fine-tune 后生成 d1-d3，提取 19 特征 + RF 分类。验证 depth signal 是否为 BOS-seeded 无条件生成的 artifact。\\n\",\n236\t    \"results\": {\n237\t      \"four_class_acc_rf\": 0.5,\n238\t      \"four_class_acc_rf_ci\": [\n239\t        0.48,\n240\t        0.52\n241\t      ],\n242\t      \"four_class_acc_lr\": 0.46,\n243\t      \"d0v1_auc\": 0.93,\n244\t      \"d1v2_auc\": 0.58,\n245\t      \"d2v3_auc\": 0.54,\n246\t      \"d1v3_auc\": 0.77,\n247\t      \"three_class_acc\": 0.4,\n248\t      \"three_class_acc_ci\": [\n249\t        0.38,\n250\t        0.42\n251\t      ],\n252\t      \"acc_retention_vs_bos_pct\": 58.6,\n253\t      \"acc_retention_vs_bos_pct_range\": [\n254\t        55,\n255\t        62\n256\t      ],\n257\t      \"edd_at_075\": 1,\n258\t      \"edd_at_070\": 1,\n259\t      \"feature_top5_predicted\": [\n260\t        \"p90_ppl\",\n261\t        \"var_surprisal\",\n262\t        \"mean_ppl\",\n263\t        \"mean_surprisal\",\n264\t        \"p75_ppl\"\n265\t      ],\n266\t      \"feature_importance_structure_preserved\": true,\n267\t      \"feature_importance_magnitude_attenuation_pct\": 35,\n268\t      \"per_class_recall\": {\n269\t        \"d0\": 0.88,\n270\t        \"d1\": 0.42,\n271\t        \"d2\": 0.28,\n272\t        \"d3\": 0.42\n273\t      },\n274\t      \"bos_reference_acc\": 0.854,\n275\t      \"prompted_acc\": 0.5,\n276\t      \"delta_pp\": -35.4,\n277\t      \"finetune_loss_d0\": 2.1,\n278\t      \"finetune_loss_d1\": 1.65,\n279\t      \"finetune_loss_d2\": 1.35,\n280\t      \"finetune_loss_d3\": 1.15\n281\t    },\n282\t    \"tables\": [\n283\t      {\n284\t        \"name\": \"Table S4: Prompted vs BOS-seeded accuracy (GPT-2 XL nucleus)\",\n285\t        \"columns\": [\n286\t          \"condition\",\n287\t          \"4class_acc\",\n288\t          \"d1v2_auc\",\n289\t          \"d2v3_auc\",\n290\t          \"edd_075\",\n291\t          \"retention_pct\"\n292\t        ],\n293\t        \"rows\": [\n294\t          [\n295\t            \"BOS-seeded\",\n296\t            0.854,\n297\t            0.937,\n298\t            0.882,\n299\t            3,\n300\t            100\n301\t          ],\n302\t          [\n303\t            \"Prompted (worst)\",\n304\t            0.5,\n305\t            0.58,\n306\t            0.54,\n307\t            1,\n308\t            58.6\n309\t          ],\n310\t          [\n311\t            \"Delta\",\n312\t            -0.354,\n313\t            -0.357,\n314\t            -0.342,\n315\t            -2,\n316\t            null\n317\t          ]\n318\t        ]\n319\t      },\n320\t      {\n321\t        \"name\": \"Table S5: Prompted per-class recall vs BOS\",\n322\t        \"columns\": [\n323\t          \"depth\",\n324\t          \"bos_recall\",\n325\t          \"prompted_recall\",\n326\t          \"delta\"\n327\t        ],\n328\t        \"rows\": [\n329\t          [\n330\t            \"d0\",\n331\t            0.996,\n332\t            0.88,\n333\t            -0.116\n334\t          ],\n335\t          [\n336\t            \"d1\",\n337\t            0.816,\n338\t            0.42,\n339\t            -0.396\n340\t          ],\n341\t          [\n342\t            \"d2\",\n343\t            0.596,\n344\t            0.28,\n345\t            -0.316\n346\t          ],\n347\t          [\n348\t            \"d3\",\n349\t            0.754,\n350\t            0.42,\n351\t            -0.334\n352\t          ]\n353\t        ]\n354\t      },\n355\t      {\n356\t        \"name\": \"Table S6: Finetune loss comparison\",\n357\t        \"columns\": [\n358\t          \"depth\",\n359\t          \"bos_loss\",\n360\t          \"prompted_loss\",\n361\t          \"delta\"\n362\t        ],\n363\t        \"rows\": [\n364\t          [\n365\t            \"d0\",\n366\t            2.55,\n367\t            2.1,\n368\t            -0.45\n369\t          ],\n370\t          [\n371\t            \"d1\",\n372\t            1.72,\n373\t            1.65,\n374\t            -0.07\n375\t          ],\n376\t          [\n377\t            \"d2\",\n378\t            1.29,\n379\t            1.35,\n380\t            0.06\n381\t          ],\n382\t          [\n383\t            \"d3\",\n384\t            null,\n385\t            1.15,\n386\t            null\n387\t          ]\n388\t        ]\n389\t      }\n390\t    ],\n391\t    \"figures\": [],\n392\t    \"analysis\": \"Prompted generation 在 worst tier 下证实了 ecological validity 核心假设失败： depth signal 高度依赖 BOS-seeded 无条件生成模式。50% accuracy（vs BOS 85.4%） 意味着 prompted 条件下分类器只比 chance 高 25pp，而 BOS 条件下高 60pp—— 超过 60% 的相对信号在 prompted 模式下消失。\\n叙事处理：此结果写入 Section 6 \\\"Boundary Conditions of the Depth Signal\\\" 的 Generation Mode Dimension。关键措辞：\\\"The depth signal is substantially attenuated under prompted (topic-seeded) generation — 4-class accuracy drops from 85.4% (BOS-seeded) to 50.0% (prompted), with EDD collapsing from 3 to 1. This indicates that a significant portion of the BOS-seeded depth signal arises from the unconstrained distributional freedom of unconditional generation, which LoRA fine-tuning can fully exploit at each depth iteration. Prompted generation constrains this freedom, compressing the per-depth distributional shift and reducing the feature-space gradient available to classifiers.\\\"\\n好消息：feature importance 结构保留（p90_ppl/var_surprisal 仍 top-2），说明 信号的性质不变（同类特征仍最有信息量），只是幅度衰减。这支持\\\"信号是真实的但 脆弱的\\\"叙事，而非\\\"信号是 artifact\\\"。\\n对论文定位的影响：Claim 1 必须退到 \\\"feasible under controlled conditions\\\"， ecological validity 成为一个明确的 boundary condition 而非已解决的问题。 这与 \\\"diagnostic/boundary characterization paper\\\" 定位一致。\\n\\n\\nWorst tier 核心机制：prompted generation 从根本上改变了 perplexity 特征的信号 结构，使 depth gradient 严重衰减。\\n具体机制链：\\n(1) Prompt anchoring effect：topic prompt 前缀（\\\"The following article discusses climate change...\\\"等）约束了生成文本的词汇分布和主题范围。BOS-seeded 生成是 完全无条件的——模型从空白开始，每个深度的分布偏移完整体现在输出中。Prompted 生成中，prompt 提供了一个 distributional anchor，LoRA fine-tuning 在每个深度 迭代中需要同时 (a) 适配 prompt-conditioned 分布 和 (b) 引入深度相关的偏移。 这两个目标部分冲突——prompt anchor 限制了可偏移的分布空间。\\n(2) Perplexity floor effect：Pythia-160M 对 prompted text 的 perplexity 整体 更低且更集中（因为 prompt 提供了上下文，Pythia 的下文预测更准），导致 p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 的动态范围被压缩。具体来说，BOS-seeded d0 的 p90_ppl ≈ 180-220， 但 prompted d0 可能只有 120-150（prompt 提供了 context），深度梯度的绝对变化量 从 ~80 points 压缩到 ~30 points，信噪比下降约 60%。\\n(3) Feature importance 结构保留但幅度衰减：p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 仍在 top-5 （不同于 13B 的结构性破坏），因为 prompted generation 不改变哪些特征有信息量， 只是缩小了信息量的幅度。这是 worst tier 中一个\\\"不是最差\\\"的维度——prompted 的 问题是信号衰减而非信号结构破坏。\\n(4) d1v2 AUC 0.58 的来源：depth-1 和 depth-2 的 prompted 输出在 Pythia 视角 下几乎不可区分，因为 LoRA 在 prompted 条件下的 per-depth 分布偏移量更小（loss convergence gap d1-d2 仅 0.30 vs BOS 模式下的 0.84）。prompt 的 constraint 使得连续深度的输出分布差异主要体现在远离 prompt 的 token 位置，而特征提取 使用固定 truncation length（498 tokens），可能截断了信号最强的尾部区域。\\n(5) 58.6% retention 意味着 prompted 条件下约 41% 的信号丢失。GPT-2 XL 是 1-1.5B 中信号最强的（85.4%），如果它在 prompted 模式下降到 50%，那么 Pythia 和 OLMo 在 prompted 模式下可能只有 40-45%，接近 chance。这使得 \\\"depth signal persists under prompted generation\\\" 的 Claim 1 表述不可持续。\\n(6) EDD=1（T=0.75 和 T=0.70）意味着在 prompted 条件下只有 d0v1 boundary 可靠，depth estimation 退化为 binary real-vs-synthetic detection，与 13B worst tier 的结论一致。\\n\"\n393\t  },\n394\t  {\n395\t    \"name\": \"Cross-strategy two-stage pipeline (strategy clf + conditioned depth)\",\n396\t    \"description\": \"两阶段方案：(a) 19 特征 → 3-class strategy classifier (nucleus/temp/topk)， (b) 识别策略后用策略专属 RF 估深度。解决 59.1% 跨策略准确率问题。\\n\",\n397\t    \"results\": {\n398\t      \"strategy_clf_overall_acc\": 0.575,\n399\t      \"strategy_clf_per_model\": {\n400\t        \"pythia\": 0.523,\n401\t        \"olmo\": 0.548,\n402\t        \"gpt2xl\": 0.654\n403\t      },\n404\t      \"strategy_clf_per_strategy_recall\": {\n405\t        \"nucleus\": 0.662,\n406\t        \"temp09\": 0.467,\n407\t        \"topk50\": 0.597\n408\t      },\n409\t      \"predicted_two_stage_acc\": {\n410\t        \"pythia\": 0.693,\n411\t        \"olmo\": 0.695,\n412\t        \"gpt2xl\": 0.73,\n413\t        \"mean\": 0.706\n414\t      },\n415\t      \"naive_pooled_acc\": {\n416\t        \"pythia\": 0.709,\n417\t        \"olmo\": 0.712,\n418\t        \"gpt2xl\": 0.739,\n419\t        \"mean\": 0.72\n420\t      },\n421\t      \"oracle_two_stage_acc\": {\n422\t        \"pythia\": 0.746,\n423\t        \"olmo\": 0.785,\n424\t        \"gpt2xl\": 0.82,\n425\t        \"mean\": 0.784\n426\t      },\n427\t      \"within_strategy_ref_acc\": {\n428\t        \"pythia\": 0.745,\n429\t        \"olmo\": 0.784,\n430\t        \"gpt2xl\": 0.816,\n431\t        \"mean\": 0.782\n432\t      },\n433\t      \"predicted_vs_naive_gap_pp\": -1.4,\n434\t      \"oracle_vs_within_gap_pp\": 0.2,\n435\t      \"strategy_clf_bottleneck\": true,\n436\t      \"temp09_clf_recall\": 0.467,\n437\t      \"temp09_misclass_as_nucleus_pct\": 38\n438\t    },\n439\t    \"tables\": [\n440\t      {\n441\t        \"name\": \"Table S7: Two-stage pipeline accuracy decomposition\",\n442\t        \"columns\": [\n443\t          \"condition\",\n444\t          \"pythia\",\n445\t          \"olmo\",\n446\t          \"gpt2xl\",\n447\t          \"mean\"\n448\t        ],\n449\t        \"rows\": [\n450\t          [\n451\t            \"Cross-strategy LOO (baseline)\",\n452\t            0.612,\n453\t            0.595,\n454\t            0.566,\n455\t            0.591\n456\t          ],\n457\t          [\n458\t            \"Naive pooled\",\n459\t            0.709,\n460\t            0.712,\n461\t            0.739,\n462\t            0.72\n463\t          ],\n464\t          [\n465\t            \"Predicted two-stage\",\n466\t            0.693,\n467\t            0.695,\n468\t            0.73,\n469\t            0.706\n470\t          ],\n471\t          [\n472\t            \"Oracle two-stage\",\n473\t            0.746,\n474\t            0.785,\n475\t            0.82,\n476\t            0.784\n477\t          ],\n478\t          [\n479\t            \"Within-strategy (ceiling)\",\n480\t            0.745,\n481\t            0.784,\n482\t            0.816,\n483\t            0.782\n484\t          ]\n485\t        ]\n486\t      },\n487\t      {\n488\t        \"name\": \"Table S8: Strategy classification confusion matrix (3-model mean)\",\n489\t        \"columns\": [\n490\t          \"true/predicted\",\n491\t          \"nucleus\",\n492\t          \"temp09\",\n493\t          \"topk50\"\n494\t        ],\n495\t        \"rows\": [\n496\t          [\n497\t            \"nucleus\",\n498\t            0.662,\n499\t            0.182,\n500\t            0.156\n501\t          ],\n502\t          [\n503\t            \"temp09\",\n504\t            0.38,\n505\t            0.467,\n506\t            0.153\n507\t          ],\n508\t          [\n509\t            \"topk50\",\n510\t            0.163,\n511\t            0.24,\n512\t            0.597\n513\t          ]\n514\t        ]\n515\t      }\n516\t    ],\n517\t    \"figures\": [],\n518\t    \"analysis\": \"Two-stage pipeline 在 worst tier 下证实了 Claim 3 的失败：strategy classifier 的 57.5% 准确率是结构性瓶颈，不是可以通过调参或更多数据解决的——19 个特征 从设计上就不携带足够的策略判别信息。Pipeline 不仅没有改善跨策略性能，反而因为 misrouting penalty 比 naive pooling 差 1.4pp。\\n对论文结构的影响：Claim 3 从独立 contribution 降为 Discussion future work， 措辞改为 \\\"We explored a two-stage strategy-aware pipeline and found that while oracle strategy identification perfectly recovers within-strategy accuracy (78.4% vs 78.2%), strategy classification from the same 19 perplexity features reaches only 57.5% — insufficient to outperform naive pooling (70.6% vs 72.0%). This reveals that perplexity summary statistics, while effective for depth discrimination, do not carry sufficient information to distinguish decoding strategies. Future work should explore strategy-specific features (e.g., token-level probability distributions, softmax entropy profiles) for the first stage.\\\"\\nOracle 结果（78.4% ≈ within-strategy 78.2%）本身是有价值的 finding——它证明 跨策略问题的根源完全是策略混淆而非深度信号的策略依赖性。这与 temperature 反转分析（Section 6 的 Strategy Dimension）一致：策略不是 noise，而是信号的 structural moderator。策略已知时，信号完全可恢复。\\n但在 worst tier 叙事下，这个 positive oracle 结果只能作为 \\\"theoretical validation\\\" 写入 Discussion，不能撑起一个独立 Claim。论文退到两个 Claims： Claim 1（bounded feasibility）+ Claim 2（Atlas/EDD, PRIMARY）。\\n\\nWorst tier 核心问题：strategy classifier 准确率仅 57.5%（chance=33.3%）， 远低于预期的 >90%，导致 predicted two-stage（70.6%）反而低于 naive pooled （72.0%），pipeline 无实际价值。\\n机制分析：\\n(1) 策略不可分性的根因：19 个 perplexity/surprisal 统计特征的设计目的是 捕捉深度信号，不是策略信号。深度梯度（across depths within a strategy）远大于 策略梯度（across strategies within a depth）——这恰恰是深度估计成功的原因， 但也是策略分类失败的原因。三种策略在 depth-0 上使用相同 base model 生成， 特征完全相同；depth-1+ 的策略差异主要体现在 token-level 分布形状（nucleus 截断 vs temperature 缩放 vs topk 截断），而 19 个 summary statistics 将 500 tokens 的 token-level 信息压缩为单个数值，丢失了大部分策略判别信息。\\n(2) Temperature 最难分类（recall 46.7%）：temperature sampling 的均匀 logit 缩放不改变 token rank order，只改变 softmax 后的概率分布平滑度。在 Pythia reference model 的 perplexity 视角下，这种平滑度变化被 mean_ppl 和 p90_ppl 部分吸收但不够 distinctive——temperature 的很多样本在特征空间中落入 nucleus 和 topk 的重叠区域。38% 的 temp09 样本被误分为 nucleus，因为两者的 perplexity 尾部分布高度相似（nucleus 截断概率 < 0.05 的 tokens，temperature 降低但保留 所有 tokens 的概率——在 Pythia 眼中，两者都产生 \\\"somewhat surprising\\\" 的输出）。\\n(3) Predicted < Naive 的数学原因：设 strategy clf error rate = e ≈ 0.425。 误分类的样本被送入错误的 strategy-conditioned depth classifier，其性能等于 cross-strategy LOO 水平（~59%）。正确分类的样本使用 within-strategy classifier （~78%）。加权平均：0.575 × 0.78 + 0.425 × 0.59 = 0.449 + 0.251 = 0.700 ≈ 70.6%。 Naive pooled（全部数据 train single RF）≈ 72%，因为 pooling 虽然模糊了策略边界， 但避免了 misrouting 的惩罚。当 strategy clf acc < ~75% 时，two-stage 数学上 必然劣于 naive pooled。\\n(4) Oracle vs within-strategy gap 仅 0.2pp（78.4% vs 78.2%），完美验证了 理论：如果策略已知，conditioned depth estimation 可以完全恢复 within-strategy 性能。但这是 oracle 条件——现实中策略未知，pipeline 的瓶颈完全在策略识别环节。\\n(5) Worst tier 结论：strategy classification 准确率无法超过 60%（因为 19 个 特征的设计先天不适合策略判别），predicted two-stage 始终 ≤ naive pooled， pipeline 无实际部署价值。Claim 3 不具备作为独立 contribution 的条件。\\n\"\n519\t  }\n520\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e0d3815-f5c2-419a-a028-0e345e283d74","uuid":"171ead84-43f9-4ca8-9734-bc9ac42806ef","timestamp":"2026-05-17T08:37:16.459Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_2/projects/recursive_gen_depth_est/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T075852/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DCOL component ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"DCOL v6 (RoBERTa-large) 失败后前置条件 plan_004 未满足，此实验已取消。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"cancelled\",\n      \"reason\": \"DCOL v6 conclusion=negative (test_acc=64.5% vs RF baseline 78.2%, -13.7pp)，无可消融的成功模型\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"plan_010 取消对论文无影响。DCOL 失败本身写入 negative analysis section（约 0.5 页）， 论述\\\"为何 contrastive ordinal learning 在此 task 上比 feature engineering 差\\\"。 这反而强化 Atlas（Claim 2）的 primary 定位——统计特征方法的优越性不是因为缺乏更好方法， 而是因为任务特性（稀疏信号、微弱梯度）使端到端学习困难。\\n\\n\\nDCOL v1-v6 全线失败，最好结果仅 64.5%（RoBERTa-large v6），远低于 RF baseline。 contrastive ordinal learning 在文本深度估计上存在固有困难：(1) 文本嵌入空间的深度梯度 远弱于 19 维统计特征空间中的梯度，(2) 端到端学习需要从原始文本中同时学习特征提取和序数 排列，数据量不足以支撑。消融无意义——没有成功的完整模型可以消融。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"13B clean FP16 scale validation (Qwen2.5-14B)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-14B FP16 + LoRA on 96GB RTX PRO 6000，nucleus p=0.95 decoding， d0-d3 递归链 + Pythia-160M reference model 19 特征提取 + RF/LR 分类。 验证 depth signal 在主流模型规模上是否持续。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"four_class_acc_rf\": 0.55,\n      \"four_class_acc_rf_ci\": [\n        0.53,\n        0.57\n      ],\n      \"four_class_acc_lr\": 0.51,\n      \"d0v1_auc\": 0.96,\n      \"d1v2_auc\": 0.62,\n      \"d2v3_auc\": 0.56,\n      \"d1v3_auc\": 0.81,\n      \"three_class_acc\": 0.44,\n      \"three_class_acc_ci\": [\n        0.42,\n        0.46\n      ],\n      \"edd_at_075\": 1,\n      \"edd_at_070\": 2,\n      \"feature_top2_in_top4\": false,\n      \"top_features_predicted\": [\n        \"mean_ppl\",\n        \"p75_ppl\",\n        \"type_token_ratio\",\n        \"rep_3gram\",\n        \"p90_ppl\"\n      ],\n      \"u_shape_artifact\": true,\n      \"u_shape_pattern\": \"d1v2=0.62, d2v3=0.56 (trough), possible d2v3 < d3v4 recovery\",\n      \"finetune_loss_d0\": 1.85,\n      \"finetune_loss_d1\": 1.52,\n      \"finetune_loss_d2\": 1.38,\n      \"finetune_loss_d3\": 1.31,\n      \"loss_convergence_gap_d1_d2\": 0.14,\n      \"per_class_recall\": {\n        \"d0\": 0.93,\n        \"d1\": 0.48,\n        \"d2\": 0.32,\n        \"d3\": 0.47\n      },\n      \"acc_vs_best_1_5b_retention_pct\": 64.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S1: 13B vs 1-1.5B 4-class accuracy comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"model\",\n          \"scale\",\n          \"4class_acc_rf\",\n          \"d1v2_auc\",\n          \"d2v3_auc\",\n          \"edd_075\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pythia-1.4B\",\n            \"1.4B\",\n            0.782,\n            0.861,\n            0.801,\n            3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OLMo-1B\",\n            \"1B\",\n            0.788,\n            0.867,\n            0.812,\n            3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GPT-2 XL\",\n            \"1.5B\",\n            0.833,\n            0.913,\n            0.883,\n            3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-14B\",\n            \"14B\",\n            0.55,\n            0.62,\n            0.56,\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen-7B (QLoRA ref)\",\n            \"7B\",\n            0.601,\n            0.729,\n            0.709,\n            \">5 (U-shape)\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S2: 13B feature importance vs 1-1.5B consensus\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"rank\",\n          \"1-1.5B consensus\",\n          \"13B predicted\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            \"p90_ppl / var_surprisal\",\n            \"mean_ppl\"\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"var_surprisal / p90_ppl\",\n            \"p75_ppl\"\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            \"mean_ppl / p75_ppl\",\n            \"type_token_ratio\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"mean_surprisal\",\n            \"rep_3gram\"\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            \"p75_ppl / mean_ppl\",\n            \"p90_ppl\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"13B 结果证实 worst tier 核心假设：Pythia reference model 对大规模模型输出的 perplexity 特征区分力本质受限。55% 4-class accuracy 虽然显著高于 chance（25%）， 但相比 1-1.5B 的 70-85% 有 >20pp 衰减。更关键的是 EDD=1，意味着 ordinal depth estimation 在 13B 条件下实质退化为 binary detection。\\n叙事处理：此结果不写入 Limitations，而是写入 Section 6 \\\"Boundary Conditions\\\" 的 Scale Dimension 子节。结论：\\\"feature-based depth estimation captures a real signal at 14B scale (55% vs 25% chance, p<0.001), but the signal is severely attenuated compared to 1-1.5B, with EDD collapsing from 3 to 1. The primary bottleneck is the cross-scale perplexity measurement gap: a 160M reference model's perplexity landscape compresses the depth gradient of 14B outputs.\\\"\\n这为 future work 指出明确方向：(1) scale-matched reference models（用 7B 作为 14B 的 reference），(2) reference-free features（但 reference_free_baseline_001 已证明 reference-free 在 1-1.5B 上就差 25pp），(3) 直接使用 14B 自身的 internal representations 而非外部 perplexity。\\n\\n\\nWorst tier 核心机制：Pythia-160M reference model 对 14B 输出的 perplexity 特征 区分力严重不足。14B 模型的词汇分布远比 1-1.5B 复杂——Pythia-160M 对所有 14B 输出 都给出极高 perplexity（因为 14B 的选词模式超出 160M 的建模能力），导致 p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 的深度梯度被压缩到一个高 perplexity plateau 上，信噪比骤降。\\n具体机制链：(1) Qwen2.5-14B 的 BPE 词表（151K tokens）与 Pythia 词表（50K tokens） 不匹配，Pythia 需要更多 subword tokens 来编码 14B 的输出，系统性地膨胀 perplexity baseline；(2) 14B 模型容量大，LoRA rank=16 的微调在每个深度迭代中只轻微扰动模型—— finetune loss 序列 1.85→1.52→1.38→1.31 的衰减斜率远小于 1-1.5B 的 2.2→1.4→1.0， 说明 14B 的 LoRA 适配器修改的分布偏移量远小于小模型；(3) 由于每步分布偏移小， Pythia 测量到的深度间特征差异在噪声水平附近——d1v2 AUC 仅 0.62，d2v3 仅 0.56。\\nU-shape artifact 的来源：与 Qwen 7B（cross_scale_qwen7b_001, U-shape confirmed） 同源。d2v3 出现 trough 是因为 depth-2 和 depth-3 的 LoRA 叠加效应使模型在某些 高频 token 上出现非单调的 logit 变化，Pythia 的 perplexity 在这些位置产生混淆信号。 Llama3 8B base 也出现了 U-shape（d2v3=0.68, d3v4=0.73 recovery），进一步支持 这是跨规模特征迁移的系统性问题而非 Qwen 特有。\\nFeature importance 结构破坏：p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 不再占据 top-2，因为在高 perplexity plateau 上，尾部统计量的信噪比下降最快。mean_ppl 和 p75_ppl 因为 信号更平滑反而排名上升，但整体区分力弱。\\nEDD=1（T=0.75）意味着只有 d0v1 可靠区分，即 13B 条件下 depth estimation 实质 退化为 binary real-vs-synthetic detection。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Wild-data calibration on RedPajama/Dolma\",\n    \"description\": \"在 RedPajama 和 Dolma 真实 web 数据上评估训练好的 depth classifiers 的 calibration 和 false positive rate。验证 controlled-setting 训练的分类器在 wild data 上的可靠性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"redpajama_n_passages\": 5000,\n      \"redpajama_d0_pct\": 72.0,\n      \"redpajama_fpr_pct\": 28.0,\n      \"redpajama_d1_pct\": 18.5,\n      \"redpajama_d2_pct\": 5.8,\n      \"redpajama_d3_pct\": 3.7,\n      \"dolma_n_passages\": 5000,\n      \"dolma_d0_pct\": 76.5,\n      \"dolma_fpr_pct\": 23.5,\n      \"dolma_d1_pct\": 16.2,\n      \"dolma_d2_pct\": 4.3,\n      \"dolma_d3_pct\": 3.0,\n      \"cross_model_fpr_range_pp\": 18,\n      \"mean_p_d0_redpajama\": 0.68,\n      \"mean_p_d0_dolma\": 0.72,\n      \"pythia_fpr\": 28.0,\n      \"gpt2xl_fpr\": 30.5,\n      \"olmo_fpr\": 12.0,\n      \"calibration_brier_score\": 0.28\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S3: Wild-data FPR across datasets and reference models\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"dataset\",\n          \"pythia_fpr\",\n          \"gpt2xl_fpr\",\n          \"olmo_fpr\",\n          \"mean_fpr\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"WikiText-103\",\n            0.0,\n            1.4,\n            1.5,\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OpenWebText\",\n            0.9,\n            1.4,\n            2.8,\n            1.7\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C4\",\n            20.2,\n            22.4,\n            4.7,\n            15.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FineWeb\",\n            19.5,\n            \"~20\",\n            \"~5\",\n            \"~15\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"RedPajama (predicted)\",\n            28.0,\n            30.5,\n            12.0,\n            23.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Dolma (predicted)\",\n            25.0,\n            27.0,\n            10.0,\n            20.7\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Wild-data 结果在 worst tier 下强化 \\\"boundary conditions\\\" 叙事的第四维度： domain shift。Controlled-setting 分类器在 editorial-quality 数据上表现优异 （WikiText FPR<2%），但在 web-crawl 数据上 FPR 高达 23-30%，且 reference model 依赖性强。\\n这不会进入论文主体（plan_015 延后到 AAAI），但如果包含，应写入 Section 6 \\\"Boundary Conditions\\\" 的 Domain Dimension：depth signal 的第四个衰减边界。 与 scale（>1.5B attenuation）、generation mode（prompted attenuation）、 depth（EDD=4）并列。\\n对 EMNLP 投稿的影响：不纳入此实验是正确决策。Wild-data calibration 的复杂度 足以支撑一篇独立 follow-up 论文，强行塞入当前论文会分散 Atlas 核心贡献的注意力。\\n\\n\\nWorst tier 预期 FPR 在 23-30% 范围，与已有 wild data 结果一致但偏高端。\\n机制分析：(1) RedPajama 包含大量 CommonCrawl 数据，其中 template content、 SEO 文本、自动生成的产品描述占比显著。这些文本的统计特征（高 rep_3gram/rep_4gram、 低 type_token_ratio、异常 p90_ppl）与递归生成文本在特征空间中重叠，导致误分类。 已有证据：C4 FPR=20.2%（Pythia）、FineWeb FPR=19.5%，但 RedPajama 的 CommonCrawl 质量过滤比 C4 更宽松，预期 FPR 更高。\\n(2) Dolma 由 AI2 策划，含 CommonCrawl + Wikipedia + Books + GitHub + arXiv 等 多域混合。Wikipedia/Books 子集 FPR 极低（参考 WikiText 0% FPR），但 CommonCrawl 子集拉高整体 FPR。混合后预期 FPR ~23.5%。\\n(3) Cross-model FPR 一致性差（range=18pp）是因为不同 reference model 的 perplexity landscape 对 web 噪声的敏感度不同——OLMo 在 Dolma 上训练（域匹配），FPR 较低（参考 olmo_calibration_001 C4 FPR=4.7%），而 Pythia/GPT-2 XL 域失配导致 FPR 飙升。\\n(4) Calibration 差（Brier score 0.28）说明分类器的置信度在 wild data 上不可靠， 限制了任何基于预测概率的 graduated curation 方案。\\n这些结果证实：controlled-setting 训练的分类器在 wild data 部署面临严重的 domain shift 问题，FPR 的高方差（12-30% 取决于 reference model）使得实际部署需要 domain-specific calibration，大幅限制了 Claim 1 的 practical applicability。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Prompted generation ecological validity (GPT-2 XL, topic-seeded)\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-2 XL nucleus p=0.95，用 topic prompt 前缀（\\\"The following article discusses...\\\"等） 生成 d0，LoRA fine-tune 后生成 d1-d3，提取 19 特征 + RF 分类。验证 depth signal 是否为 BOS-seeded 无条件生成的 artifact。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"four_class_acc_rf\": 0.5,\n      \"four_class_acc_rf_ci\": [\n        0.48,\n        0.52\n      ],\n      \"four_class_acc_lr\": 0.46,\n      \"d0v1_auc\": 0.93,\n      \"d1v2_auc\": 0.58,\n      \"d2v3_auc\": 0.54,\n      \"d1v3_auc\": 0.77,\n      \"three_class_acc\": 0.4,\n      \"three_class_acc_ci\": [\n        0.38,\n        0.42\n      ],\n      \"acc_retention_vs_bos_pct\": 58.6,\n      \"acc_retention_vs_bos_pct_range\": [\n        55,\n        62\n      ],\n      \"edd_at_075\": 1,\n      \"edd_at_070\": 1,\n      \"feature_top5_predicted\": [\n        \"p90_ppl\",\n        \"var_surprisal\",\n        \"mean_ppl\",\n        \"mean_surprisal\",\n        \"p75_ppl\"\n      ],\n      \"feature_importance_structure_preserved\": true,\n      \"feature_importance_magnitude_attenuation_pct\": 35,\n      \"per_class_recall\": {\n        \"d0\": 0.88,\n        \"d1\": 0.42,\n        \"d2\": 0.28,\n        \"d3\": 0.42\n      },\n      \"bos_reference_acc\": 0.854,\n      \"prompted_acc\": 0.5,\n      \"delta_pp\": -35.4,\n      \"finetune_loss_d0\": 2.1,\n      \"finetune_loss_d1\": 1.65,\n      \"finetune_loss_d2\": 1.35,\n      \"finetune_loss_d3\": 1.15\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S4: Prompted vs BOS-seeded accuracy (GPT-2 XL nucleus)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"4class_acc\",\n          \"d1v2_auc\",\n          \"d2v3_auc\",\n          \"edd_075\",\n          \"retention_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"BOS-seeded\",\n            0.854,\n            0.937,\n            0.882,\n            3,\n            100\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Prompted (worst)\",\n            0.5,\n            0.58,\n            0.54,\n            1,\n            58.6\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Delta\",\n            -0.354,\n            -0.357,\n            -0.342,\n            -2,\n            null\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S5: Prompted per-class recall vs BOS\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"depth\",\n          \"bos_recall\",\n          \"prompted_recall\",\n          \"delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"d0\",\n            0.996,\n            0.88,\n            -0.116\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d1\",\n            0.816,\n            0.42,\n            -0.396\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d2\",\n            0.596,\n            0.28,\n            -0.316\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d3\",\n            0.754,\n            0.42,\n            -0.334\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S6: Finetune loss comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"depth\",\n          \"bos_loss\",\n          \"prompted_loss\",\n          \"delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"d0\",\n            2.55,\n            2.1,\n            -0.45\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d1\",\n            1.72,\n            1.65,\n            -0.07\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d2\",\n            1.29,\n            1.35,\n            0.06\n          ],\n          [\n            \"d3\",\n            null,\n            1.15,\n            null\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Prompted generation 在 worst tier 下证实了 ecological validity 核心假设失败： depth signal 高度依赖 BOS-seeded 无条件生成模式。50% accuracy（vs BOS 85.4%） 意味着 prompted 条件下分类器只比 chance 高 25pp，而 BOS 条件下高 60pp—— 超过 60% 的相对信号在 prompted 模式下消失。\\n叙事处理：此结果写入 Section 6 \\\"Boundary Conditions of the Depth Signal\\\" 的 Generation Mode Dimension。关键措辞：\\\"The depth signal is substantially attenuated under prompted (topic-seeded) generation — 4-class accuracy drops from 85.4% (BOS-seeded) to 50.0% (prompted), with EDD collapsing from 3 to 1. This indicates that a significant portion of the BOS-seeded depth signal arises from the unconstrained distributional freedom of unconditional generation, which LoRA fine-tuning can fully exploit at each depth iteration. Prompted generation constrains this freedom, compressing the per-depth distributional shift and reducing the feature-space gradient available to classifiers.\\\"\\n好消息：feature importance 结构保留（p90_ppl/var_surprisal 仍 top-2），说明 信号的性质不变（同类特征仍最有信息量），只是幅度衰减。这支持\\\"信号是真实的但 脆弱的\\\"叙事，而非\\\"信号是 artifact\\\"。\\n对论文定位的影响：Claim 1 必须退到 \\\"feasible under controlled conditions\\\"， ecological validity 成为一个明确的 boundary condition 而非已解决的问题。 这与 \\\"diagnostic/boundary characterization paper\\\" 定位一致。\\n\\n\\nWorst tier 核心机制：prompted generation 从根本上改变了 perplexity 特征的信号 结构，使 depth gradient 严重衰减。\\n具体机制链：\\n(1) Prompt anchoring effect：topic prompt 前缀（\\\"The following article discusses climate change...\\\"等）约束了生成文本的词汇分布和主题范围。BOS-seeded 生成是 完全无条件的——模型从空白开始，每个深度的分布偏移完整体现在输出中。Prompted 生成中，prompt 提供了一个 distributional anchor，LoRA fine-tuning 在每个深度 迭代中需要同时 (a) 适配 prompt-conditioned 分布 和 (b) 引入深度相关的偏移。 这两个目标部分冲突——prompt anchor 限制了可偏移的分布空间。\\n(2) Perplexity floor effect：Pythia-160M 对 prompted text 的 perplexity 整体 更低且更集中（因为 prompt 提供了上下文，Pythia 的下文预测更准），导致 p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 的动态范围被压缩。具体来说，BOS-seeded d0 的 p90_ppl ≈ 180-220， 但 prompted d0 可能只有 120-150（prompt 提供了 context），深度梯度的绝对变化量 从 ~80 points 压缩到 ~30 points，信噪比下降约 60%。\\n(3) Feature importance 结构保留但幅度衰减：p90_ppl 和 var_surprisal 仍在 top-5 （不同于 13B 的结构性破坏），因为 prompted generation 不改变哪些特征有信息量， 只是缩小了信息量的幅度。这是 worst tier 中一个\\\"不是最差\\\"的维度——prompted 的 问题是信号衰减而非信号结构破坏。\\n(4) d1v2 AUC 0.58 的来源：depth-1 和 depth-2 的 prompted 输出在 Pythia 视角 下几乎不可区分，因为 LoRA 在 prompted 条件下的 per-depth 分布偏移量更小（loss convergence gap d1-d2 仅 0.30 vs BOS 模式下的 0.84）。prompt 的 constraint 使得连续深度的输出分布差异主要体现在远离 prompt 的 token 位置，而特征提取 使用固定 truncation length（498 tokens），可能截断了信号最强的尾部区域。\\n(5) 58.6% retention 意味着 prompted 条件下约 41% 的信号丢失。GPT-2 XL 是 1-1.5B 中信号最强的（85.4%），如果它在 prompted 模式下降到 50%，那么 Pythia 和 OLMo 在 prompted 模式下可能只有 40-45%，接近 chance。这使得 \\\"depth signal persists under prompted generation\\\" 的 Claim 1 表述不可持续。\\n(6) EDD=1（T=0.75 和 T=0.70）意味着在 prompted 条件下只有 d0v1 boundary 可靠，depth estimation 退化为 binary real-vs-synthetic detection，与 13B worst tier 的结论一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-strategy two-stage pipeline (strategy clf + conditioned depth)\",\n    \"description\": \"两阶段方案：(a) 19 特征 → 3-class strategy classifier (nucleus/temp/topk)， (b) 识别策略后用策略专属 RF 估深度。解决 59.1% 跨策略准确率问题。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"strategy_clf_overall_acc\": 0.575,\n      \"strategy_clf_per_model\": {\n        \"pythia\": 0.523,\n        \"olmo\": 0.548,\n        \"gpt2xl\": 0.654\n      },\n      \"strategy_clf_per_strategy_recall\": {\n        \"nucleus\": 0.662,\n        \"temp09\": 0.467,\n        \"topk50\": 0.597\n      },\n      \"predicted_two_stage_acc\": {\n        \"pythia\": 0.693,\n        \"olmo\": 0.695,\n        \"gpt2xl\": 0.73,\n        \"mean\": 0.706\n      },\n      \"naive_pooled_acc\": {\n        \"pythia\": 0.709,\n        \"olmo\": 0.712,\n        \"gpt2xl\": 0.739,\n        \"mean\": 0.72\n      },\n      \"oracle_two_stage_acc\": {\n        \"pythia\": 0.746,\n        \"olmo\": 0.785,\n        \"gpt2xl\": 0.82,\n        \"mean\": 0.784\n      },\n      \"within_strategy_ref_acc\": {\n        \"pythia\": 0.745,\n        \"olmo\": 0.784,\n        \"gpt2xl\": 0.816,\n        \"mean\": 0.782\n      },\n      \"predicted_vs_naive_gap_pp\": -1.4,\n      \"oracle_vs_within_gap_pp\": 0.2,\n      \"strategy_clf_bottleneck\": true,\n      \"temp09_clf_recall\": 0.467,\n      \"temp09_misclass_as_nucleus_pct\": 38\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S7: Two-stage pipeline accuracy decomposition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"pythia\",\n          \"olmo\",\n          \"gpt2xl\",\n          \"mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Cross-strategy LOO (baseline)\",\n            0.612,\n            0.595,\n            0.566,\n            0.591\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Naive pooled\",\n            0.709,\n            0.712,\n            0.739,\n            0.72\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Predicted two-stage\",\n            0.693,\n            0.695,\n            0.73,\n            0.706\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Oracle two-stage\",\n            0.746,\n            0.785,\n            0.82,\n            0.784\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Within-strategy (ceiling)\",\n            0.745,\n            0.784,\n            0.816,\n            0.782\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table S8: Strategy classification confusion matrix (3-model mean)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"true/predicted\",\n          \"nucleus\",\n          \"temp09\",\n          \"topk50\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"nucleus\",\n            0.662,\n            0.182,\n            0.156\n          ],\n          [\n            \"temp09\",\n            0.38,\n            0.467,\n            0.153\n          ],\n          [\n            \"topk50\",\n            0.163,\n            0.24,\n            0.597\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Two-stage pipeline 在 worst tier 下证实了 Claim 3 的失败：strategy classifier 的 57.5% 准确率是结构性瓶颈，不是可以通过调参或更多数据解决的——19 个特征 从设计上就不携带足够的策略判别信息。Pipeline 不仅没有改善跨策略性能，反而因为 misrouting penalty 比 naive pooling 差 1.4pp。\\n对论文结构的影响：Claim 3 从独立 contribution 降为 Discussion future work， 措辞改为 \\\"We explored a two-stage strategy-aware pipeline and found that while oracle strategy identification perfectly recovers within-strategy accuracy (78.4% vs 78.2%), strategy classification from the same 19 perplexity features reaches only 57.5% — insufficient to outperform naive pooling (70.6% vs 72.0%). This reveals that perplexity summary statistics, while effective for depth discrimination, do not carry sufficient information to distinguish decoding strategies. Future work should explore strategy-specific features (e.g., token-level probability distributions, softmax entropy profiles) for the first stage.\\\"\\nOracle 结果（78.4% ≈ within-strategy 78.2%）本身是有价值的 finding——它证明 跨策略问题的根源完全是策略混淆而非深度信号的策略依赖性。这与 temperature 反转分析（Section 6 的 Strategy Dimension）一致：策略不是 noise，而是信号的 structural moderator。策略已知时，信号完全可恢复。\\n但在 worst tier 叙事下，这个 positive oracle 结果只能作为 \\\"theoretical validation\\\" 写入 Discussion，不能撑起一个独立 Claim。论文退到两个 Claims： Claim 1（bounded feasibility）+ Claim 2（Atlas/EDD, PRIMARY）。\\n\\nWorst tier 核心问题：strategy classifier 准确率仅 57.5%（chance=33.3%）， 远低于预期的 >90%，导致 predicted two-stage（70.6%）反而低于 naive pooled （72.0%），pipeline 无实际价值。\\n机制分析：\\n(1) 策略不可分性的根因：19 个 perplexity/surprisal 统计特征的设计目的是 捕捉深度信号，不是策略信号。深度梯度（across depths within a strategy）远大于 策略梯度（across strategies within a depth）——这恰恰是深度估计成功的原因， 但也是策略分类失败的原因。三种策略在 depth-0 上使用相同 base model 生成， 特征完全相同；depth-1+ 的策略差异主要体现在 token-level 分布形状（nucleus 截断 vs temperature 缩放 vs topk 截断），而 19 个 summary statistics 将 500 tokens 的 token-level 信息压缩为单个数值，丢失了大部分策略判别信息。\\n(2) Temperature 最难分类（recall 46.7%）：temperature sampling 的均匀 logit 缩放不改变 token rank order，只改变 softmax 后的概率分布平滑度。在 Pythia reference model 的 perplexity 视角下，这种平滑度变化被 mean_ppl 和 p90_ppl 部分吸收但不够 distinctive——temperature 的很多样本在特征空间中落入 nucleus 和 topk 的重叠区域。38% 的 temp09 样本被误分为 nucleus，因为两者的 perplexity 尾部分布高度相似（nucleus 截断概率 < 0.05 的 tokens，temperature 降低但保留 所有 tokens 的概率——在 Pythia 眼中，两者都产生 \\\"somewhat surprising\\\" 的输出）。\\n(3) Predicted < Naive 的数学原因：设 strategy clf error rate = e ≈ 0.425。 误分类的样本被送入错误的 strategy-conditioned depth classifier，其性能等于 cross-strategy LOO 水平（~59%）。正确分类的样本使用 within-strategy classifier （~78%）。加权平均：0.575 × 0.78 + 0.425 × 0.59 = 0.449 + 0.251 = 0.700 ≈ 70.6%。 Naive pooled（全部数据 train single RF）≈ 72%，因为 pooling 虽然模糊了策略边界， 但避免了 misrouting 的惩罚。当 strategy clf acc < ~75% 时，two-stage 数学上 必然劣于 naive pooled。\\n(4) Oracle vs within-strategy gap 仅 0.2pp（78.4% vs 78.2%），完美验证了 理论：如果策略已知，conditioned depth estimation 可以完全恢复 within-strategy 性能。但这是 oracle 条件——现实中策略未知，pipeline 的瓶颈完全在策略识别环节。\\n(5) Worst tier 结论：strategy classification 准确率无法超过 60%（因为 19 个 特征的设计先天不适合策略判别），predicted two-stage 始终 ≤ naive pooled， pipeline 无实际部署价值。Claim 3 不具备作为独立 contribution 的条件。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":520,"startLine":1,"totalLines":520}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CUdSVeJdn4gmDxy1ZVHGEg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data. Let me also check if the output directory exists.\n\nLet me analyze the experiment data and paper framing to write the paper.\n\nThe experiments are:\n1. DCOL component ablation - cancelled, negative result\n2. 13B clean FP16 scale validation (Qwen2.5-14B) - shows signal attenuation at scale\n3. Wild-data calibration on RedPajama/Dolma - high FPR on web-crawl data\n4. Prompted generation ecological validity (GPT-2 XL) - signal severely attenuated under prompted generation\n\n\n5. Cross-strategy two-stage pipeline - strategy classifier bottleneck, pipeline worse than naive pooling\n\nThe narrative guidance says:\n- Reframe from \"robust framework\" to \"first systematic characterization of recursive depth phenomena and boundary conditions\"\n- Atlas (Claim 2) is the primary contribution\n- Claim 1 becomes bounded: feasible under controlled conditions (1-1.5B, BOS-seeded, within-strategy, 70-85%), but signal attenuates at larger scales and prompted generation\n- 13B weak results + prompted weak results go into Section 6 \"Boundary Conditions\"\n- Claim 3 (cross-strategy pipeline) demoted to Discussion future work\n- Paper type: diagnostic\n\nNow I'm structuring the full paper around the Atlas as the centerpiece, with the benchmark results from the 3-model × 3-strategy experiments providing the empirical foundation. I'll pull in the EDD analysis, feature importance findings, and the temperature reversal observations to support the boundary conditions narrative, while treating the cross-strategy pipeline failure as a cautionary note for future work. The DCOL results go into the negative analysis section to show where the depth signal breaks down. I'm pulling the key experimental results from the framing document to structure the Atlas section—the accuracy ranges across models and strategies, the AUC scores showing how well the detector generalizes across different model pairs, the EDD findings that suggest consistent behavior at specific temperature thresholds, and the cross-validation results that reveal both model and strategy dependencies. I'll also weave in the feature importance findings about p90_ppl and surprisal variance, plus the temperature reversal results that show how fragile some detections become under different conditions.\n\nNow I'm realizing the wild-data calibration experiment needs to be included despite the analysis suggesting it shouldn't be in the main body—I'll place it briefly in Section 6 or push it to supplementary material to satisfy the requirement that every experiment gets coverage. Let me map out the full paper structure: Abstract, Introduction, Related Work, then the formalization and methods section covering the problem definition, the recursive generation protocol, feature extraction, and classification approaches. The main Atlas section will present the controlled-setting results with the 3×3 model-strategy grid, followed by subsections on feature analysis and generalization patterns. I need to verify the data sources are accurate before writing this out, and I should check that the directory structure is set up correctly first.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4961,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11050,"cache_read_input_tokens":24419,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11050},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3e0d3815-f5c2-419a-a028-0e345e283d74","uuid":"dbb218ac-2e29-41f8-bf08-a89ff24471bd"}
